# Template for the owner-local settings of the lab tools. Copy it to ~/.config/m5-guardian/local.conf
# (or point GUARDIAN_LOCAL_CONF at your copy) and fill in your own values. Never commit the copy.
# An exported environment variable of the same name always wins over this file.
# Resolvers: tools/guardian_local.py (Python) and tools/guardian-local.sh (shell).
# A tool that needs a key you have not set refuses with the key's name; nothing falls back to a guess.

# Artifact store: builds, logs, evidence, the Ralph data. It must contain an empty file named
# .guardian-store-root.
GUARDIAN_STORE=/path/to/guardian-store
# Optional: the mount point the store lives on. When set, it must be a mounted smbfs share, so
# nothing is ever written into an empty mount point.
#GUARDIAN_STORE_MOUNT=/mnt/your-share

# Optional: a substring of CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR that the Ralph runner and the reviewer refuse to use
# (for example a work profile that must never run this project's agents).
#GUARDIAN_FORBIDDEN_CLAUDE_CONFIG=work-profile

# Lab bench identities (only the live lab tools under lab/ and tools/threat_watch.py need them).
# Addresses as six colon-separated bytes. A value runs to the end of its line: no trailing comments.
# The StickS3 under test (board runs, threat_watch):
#GUARDIAN_LAB_STICK_MAC=02:00:00:00:00:01
# The receiver / Wi-Fi client board (its USB serial number):
#GUARDIAN_LAB_CARDPUTER_MAC=02:00:00:00:00:02
# The stimulus board attached to the lab Pi:
#GUARDIAN_LAB_EMITTER_MAC=02:00:00:00:00:03
# ssh target of the lab Pi (user@host or an ~/.ssh/config alias), its Python, and the folder that
# holds emitter.py and ap_control.py on it:
#GUARDIAN_LAB_PI_SSH=lab-pi
#GUARDIAN_LAB_PI_PYTHON=/path/on/the/pi/bin/python
#GUARDIAN_LAB_PI_TOOLS=/path/on/the/pi/lab-tools
# Target of lab/live/deauth_truth.py (your own access point only):
#GUARDIAN_LAB_AP=02:00:00:00:00:04
#GUARDIAN_LAB_SSID=your-network-name
